  "descriptions": [
    {
      "description": "This component houses Structural Stability Science (SSS) governance records defining source-governed application domains, authorized-use boundaries, and domain-specific access surfaces within the SSS / DHFT / SIM / LCB architecture.\n\nRecords in this component identify domain placement, source hierarchy, non-equivalence boundaries, public-access limitations, and authorization requirements for education, legal systems, AI systems, human and somatic systems, business and organizational systems, governance and compliance systems, Spanish-language instantiation, and related application surfaces.\n\nThese records do not replace, modify, or expand the DHFT source architecture. They do not disclose the Structural Identification Method as an implementation manual and do not authorize assessment, audit, certification, training, institutional deployment, machine use, practitioner use, teacher training, implementation, or derivative method development.\n\nAll authorized use requires written authorization through Somatic Rising Institute or the source steward.",
      "descriptionType": "Abstract"
    }
  ],
